ller that has stopped installing or refreshing flows. The switch screenshot shows ","position":{"start":{"line":5,"column":1},"end":{"line":5,"column":1}},"key":"Gbgo2gMwr9"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fail_mode: secure","position":{"start":{"line":5,"column":1},"end":{"line":5,"column":1}},"key":"HaF09sx6C1"},{"type":"text","value":", so a controller that is actually gone should cause the bridge to drop packets rather than forward them. A restart of POX putting the policy back says the controller process was the piece that had stalled.","position":{"start":{"line":5,"column":1},"end":{"line":5,"column":1}},"key":"XmVB28ZoeP"}],"key":"pQSvNOvvRH"}],"key":"Jfg8ykd3sP"}],"key":"umfYP5Rvwu"},"references":{"cite":{"order":[],"data":{}}},"footer":{"navigation":{"prev":{"title":"CSE548 Advanced Network Security - Project 1 - Packet Filter Firewall","url":"/sections/mcs-projects/cse548-advanced-network-security/project-1/project-1","group":"Master's in Computer Science (Cybersecurity) Projects"},"next":{"title":"CSE543 Information Assurance and Security","url":"/sections/mcs-projects/cse543-information-assurance-and-security/cse543-information-assurance-and-security-head","group":"Master's in Computer Science (Cybersecurity) Projects"}}},"domain":"https://www.mkdynamics.net"}